# The gate cannot enforce anything about itself.
#
# `required.yml` runs from the PULL REQUEST's own head, so a PR can edit the
# workflow and the script that judge it — raise the deadline, add a conclusion
# to the allowlist, delete the canary — and the weakened gate is what reports on
# that very PR. No amount of logic inside the script closes that; review does.
#
# Same reasoning for the other instruments: claims.yaml and claim-check.py gate
# the repo's public claims, the vacuous-oracle check gates test selectors, and
# formal-verification.yml is where a `tolerate_failure` flips. An edit to any of
# them changes what "CI green" means, which is exactly the class of change that
# should not land unseen.
/.github/workflows/           @pulseengine
/.github/CODEOWNERS           @pulseengine
/verification/               @pulseengine
/claims.yaml                 @pulseengine
/rust-toolchain.toml         @pulseengine
